    "revision": 10,
    "title": "Express all, only and each",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-scope-basic-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Express all, only and each",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "都 includes every member of an identified group; 只 restricts the assertion to the focused action, thing or person. Place them before the predicate. 每…都… applies the following statement to each individual member.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我们都有书。",
                "pinyin": "wǒmen dōu yǒu shū 。",
                "meaning": "We all have books.",
                "audio": "1caa40567f607a915b418b9ef5258c6d4171c6ade65255a62ec29eee41889efa"
              },
              {
                "text": "我只看书。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ zhǐ kàn shū 。",
                "meaning": "I only read books.",
                "audio": "a0d77a92c59642c7ffae56424b343e16017c8d18362f40cb400a645ff6e4a603"
              },
              {
                "text": "每个人都有书。",
                "pinyin": "měi gè rén dōu yǒu shū 。",
                "meaning": "Every person has a book.",
                "audio": "9fed18f83257bc4b41f79ea51c95221723e7e7ab67e75f8ae5e5195cff190311"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
